slides.content:
# When Rows or Columns Are Created Automatically

If you define columns but not rows (or vice versa), the browser creates **implicit** tracks to hold items that overflow the defined grid. You can size implicit tracks with `grid-auto-rows` and `grid-auto-columns`.

```css
.container {
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr;
  grid-auto-rows: 150px; /* any extra rows will be 150px tall */
}
```
This is extremely useful for dynamic content.
